WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.541 --> 00:00:20.463
knew she should probably be panicking.

2
00:00:20.983 --> 00:00:24.185
But she couldn't help being happy about returning to the vortex.

3
00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:29.028
Except this time the vortex seemed different.

4
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.923
It was darker than usual, with fewer swirling lights.

5
00:00:33.803 --> 00:00:37.266
A deafening roar made Perda wish she could cover her ears.

6
00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:43.911
But she was using both hands to cling onto Zann's arm because they seemed to be tumbling faster

7
00:00:43.951 --> 00:00:45.012
than ever before.

8
00:00:45.032 --> 00:00:46.313
"Hold on!"

9
00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:47.995
Zann yelled over the noise.

10
00:00:48.015 --> 00:00:50.457
"I'll try to grab a wormhole."

11
00:00:51.578 --> 00:00:52.538
Perda looked around.

12
00:00:52.558 --> 00:00:54.540
"Where?" she cried.

13
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.602
"There are hardly any wormholes here!"

14
00:00:58.323 --> 00:01:01.469
For the first time, she felt a twinge of panic.

15
00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:05.072
Normally there were lots of wormholes in the vortex.

16
00:01:05.812 --> 00:01:11.896
The only tricky part was finding the one you wanted—or at least not accidentally pulling yourself out into

17
00:01:11.936 --> 00:01:13.558
a scary, dangerous world.

18
00:01:14.638 --> 00:01:18.141
But now a wormhole passed by only once every few minutes.

19
00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:19.702
"There's one!"

20
00:01:19.962 --> 00:01:20.422
she yelled.

21
00:01:20.442 --> 00:01:21.383
"Got it!"

22
00:01:22.263 --> 00:01:27.427
Zann had managed to wrap Zing's leash around his waist, so he used both hands to grab at

23
00:01:27.447 --> 00:01:28.608
the edge of the wormhole.

24
00:01:29.164 --> 00:01:30.205
Perda grabbed it too.

25
00:01:31.046 --> 00:01:35.049
She saw a steep mountainside covered with dark, dripping trees.

26
00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:42.095
The sky was dark, and jagged flashes of lightning lit up the scene every few seconds, glaring off

27
00:01:42.115 --> 00:01:43.636
the craggy cliffs overhead.

28
00:01:43.656 --> 00:01:46.018
"Weird," she commented.

29
00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:49.041
"This wormhole is in the ground too."

30
00:01:49.061 --> 00:01:52.043
"Never mind that," Zann said.

31
00:01:52.063 --> 00:01:53.784
"Are you thinking what I'm thinking?"

32
00:01:54.345 --> 00:01:55.086
Perda nodded.

33
00:01:55.106 --> 00:01:59.237
"That looks a lot like Fardark," she said with a shudder.

34
00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:04.622
They'd visited the terrifying world a couple of times and barely escaped alive.

35
00:02:05.483 --> 00:02:12.268
It was home to nothing but horrible, violent creatures who wished to harm any traveler unlucky enough to

36
00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:12.989
end up there.

37
00:02:13.009 --> 00:02:16.852
"I never saw mountains like this in Fardark though," Zann said.

38
00:02:16.872 --> 00:02:19.515
"And those trees look like some I've seen in Magica.

39
00:02:20.415 --> 00:02:21.997
Maybe it's not Fardark after all."

40
00:02:23.318 --> 00:02:25.320
"It's not worth the risk," Perda said.

41
00:02:25.976 --> 00:02:27.277
"We'll try the next world.

42
00:02:27.537 --> 00:02:30.519
But first, let's make sure we don't lose each other."

43
00:02:31.339 --> 00:02:33.600
She rubbed her fingers together to create friction.

44
00:02:34.321 --> 00:02:36.122
Then she touched Zann's arm.

45
00:02:36.162 --> 00:02:38.083
"Shackle," she said.

46
00:02:38.943 --> 00:02:41.685
Magical shackles appeared, binding them together.

47
00:02:42.425 --> 00:02:44.947
Zann quickly shackled himself to Zing as well.

48
00:02:45.827 --> 00:02:50.050
They let go and tumbled on through the strange, noisy vortex.

49
00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:56.717
For a long moment, they didn't pass any wormholes, and Perda felt panic creep through her again.

50
00:02:58.357 --> 00:03:01.218
Finally a glowing wormhole appeared up ahead.

51
00:03:02.038 --> 00:03:08.660
Once again Zann grabbed the edge with both hands and managed to pull himself and Perda halfway through.

52
00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.281
They paused and looked around.

53
00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:17.322
This time the world before them was rocky and charred, with almost no foliage.

54
00:03:17.962 --> 00:03:23.464
Then there was a screech of fury, and an enormous purple dragon flew into view.

55
00:03:24.496 --> 00:03:27.338
A second, bright red dragon was pursuing it.

56
00:03:28.159 --> 00:03:32.922
It was spitting fireballs as the first dragon dodged to try to avoid them.

57
00:03:34.222 --> 00:03:38.705
The purple dragon screamed in pain as a fireball hit it in the back of the head.

58
00:03:39.306 --> 00:03:44.889
The dragon spun around and leaped toward the other dragon with deadly claws extended.

59
00:03:44.909 --> 00:03:48.852
The two huge creatures were locked in battle.

60
00:03:49.472 --> 00:03:55.575
They tumbled to the hard ground with a thump that nearly shook loose Perda's grip on the wormhole.

61
00:03:55.595 --> 00:04:01.017
"Oh, no," she said, her heart sinking as she realized where they must be.

62
00:04:01.037 --> 00:04:03.698
"I think this is Drac!"

63
00:04:05.279 --> 00:04:06.379
Zann looked pale.

64
00:04:07.119 --> 00:04:10.681
Drac was another dangerous world they'd barely escaped.

65
00:04:11.381 --> 00:04:13.702
There, dragons were the dominant species.

66
00:04:14.522 --> 00:04:18.484
They treated humans as servants—and sometimes as food.

67
00:04:19.344 --> 00:04:21.425
Zing was peering out through the wormhole.

68
00:04:22.106 --> 00:04:25.148
He shot out a puff of smoke in the direction of the dragons.

69
00:04:25.168 --> 00:04:30.751
"That red dragon looks like a much larger version of Zing," Perda thought.

70
00:04:30.771 --> 00:04:33.513
"Maybe it's a type of fire whistler."

71
00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:38.736
She liked Zing just fine, but he could be a little destructive.

72
00:04:39.416 --> 00:04:44.319
That's why Zann was one of the few people in Magica who chose to keep a fire whistler

73
00:04:44.559 --> 00:04:45.040
as a pet.

74
00:04:45.544 --> 00:04:49.708
She couldn't even imagine what kind of damage a huge version of Zing could do!

75
00:04:49.728 --> 00:04:55.793
"Let's get out of here before they notice us," Zann said as the wrestling dragons rolled closer to

76
00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:56.473
the wormhole.

77
00:04:57.494 --> 00:05:01.757
Once again he and Perda let go and continued through the vortex.

78
00:05:02.518 --> 00:05:05.501
"We've got to find a place to stop and rest soon," Zann said.

79
00:05:06.161 --> 00:05:07.943
Perda realized he was right.

80
00:05:08.563 --> 00:05:12.827
Already she could feel the last bits of magic energy ebbing from her body.

81
00:05:13.447 --> 00:05:14.208
That was weird.

82
00:05:14.964 --> 00:05:17.845
Traveling through the vortex always used a lot of energy.

83
00:05:18.465 --> 00:05:22.067
But she'd never lost this much energy this quickly before.

84
00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:28.470
"We have to stop at the next world, no matter what," she said as another wormhole appeared up

85
00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:32.391
ahead. "Yeah," Zann agreed, sounding tired.

86
00:05:32.411 --> 00:05:35.832
"At least we already found the two scariest worlds possible."

87
00:05:36.473 --> 00:05:38.233
"Not quite," Perda said.

88
00:05:38.253 --> 00:05:41.755
"What about that world we found with no magic at all?"

89
00:05:42.295 --> 00:05:44.156
She shuddered just thinking about it.

90
00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:48.682
That world had been full of interesting sights, smells, and people.

91
00:05:49.283 --> 00:05:51.924
But there was no natural magic energy there at all.

92
00:05:52.524 --> 00:05:58.168
Perda and her friends were helpless to do even the simplest things, like create food or zap from

93
00:05:58.208 --> 00:05:58.888
place to place.

94
00:05:59.788 --> 00:06:05.492
Plus, since magic energy was required to open a wormhole, they'd almost been trapped there forever!

95
00:06:05.512 --> 00:06:08.553
"What are the odds we'd end up there again?"

96
00:06:09.214 --> 00:06:09.794
Zann said.

97
00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:13.176
He grabbed the next wormhole as it swirled past.

98
00:06:13.684 --> 00:06:16.327
Perda pulled herself up beside him to take a look.

99
00:06:16.347 --> 00:06:21.731
"At least the sun is shining here," Zann said, glancing around.

100
00:06:22.332 --> 00:06:23.113
Perda nodded.

101
00:06:23.653 --> 00:06:29.959
The land before them was drab and barren, with wispy, brownish grass covering a flat plain.

102
00:06:30.679 --> 00:06:35.904
A few boulders and prickly shrubs were the only other things breaking up the boring scene.

103
00:06:35.924 --> 00:06:40.028
"This doesn't look like a very exciting world," she said.

104
00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.768
"But I suppose it's a safe place to rest and figure out how to get back to Magica."

105
00:06:44.788 --> 00:06:46.792
"I agree," Zann said.

106
00:06:46.812 --> 00:06:47.914
"Let's go!"
